   "notes": [
    "STOP: 1 halts the oscillator, 0 lets it run. It is 0 at the first power-up and keeps its value through later power cycles. At the first power-up, writing 1 and then 0 forces the oscillator to start.",
    "10_SECOND: tens of seconds in BCD, 0 to 5. 1_SECOND: units of seconds in BCD, 0 to 9.",
    "Writing a value outside the field's range makes the clock count on from that invalid value until the counter wraps, after which it is valid again.",
    "After a return from backup to main supply the field may take up to 1 s to show the current time.",
    "Cycle: the value a bit takes when the device switches from main to backup supply; UC means unchanged.",
    "The initial value is an eight-bit value and should read 0XXXXXXXb."
   ]
  },
