    "OF: oscillator-fail flag. It latches to 1 when the 32.768-kHz oscillator misses four or more pulses in a row, is always 1 after the first power-up, and is cleared over I2C. 0: no failure seen; 1: failure seen.",
    "10_MINUTE: tens of minutes in BCD, 0 to 5. 1_MINUTE: units of minutes in BCD, 0 to 9.",
    "Writing a value outside the field's range makes the clock count on from that invalid value until the counter wraps, after which it is valid again.",
    "After a return from backup to main supply the field may take up to 1 s to show the current time.",
    "The initial value is an eight-bit value and should read 1XXXXXXXb."
