  {
   "id": "typical",
   "title": "Typical application with a backup battery",
   "page": 19,
   "description": "The clock runs from a 3.3 V VCC rail with a 1 µF ceramic capacitor across VCC and GND at the pins. A 32.768-kHz crystal sits straight across OSCI and OSCO. A BR1225 coin cell from VBACK to ground keeps the time when VCC is gone. IRQ, SCL and SDA each have a 4.7 kΩ pull-up to VCC and go out to the host controller.",
